      "writtenOn": "2021-03-11T13:26:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a tradeoff between code duplication/time and readability. For the test above, I folded it into the previous one because it could be made cleanly immediately after and it made some sense in the context of the previous test.\n\nHere, I think it would either complicate the merged test significantly (many locals to understand and more behavior to check all over) or it would simply be appended as is to save 10 lines of setup. Do consider it is also better for diagnosing flaky tests and the like if we have methods named more specifically after what they test – it\u0027s easier to understand something is wrong with handles if a test named \"forTwoProfiles\" flakes than it\u0027s a general \"testPerProfileNetworking\".\n\nWith this, I prefer to keep this separate. Please reopen if you feel strongly – in that case I will prefer the \"append\" approach for the reason that these tests are already pretty long and already have a confusingly large number of variables.",
